[~accountid:625fb4921046bb0071ddf448] apologies for the delay. Let’s summarise for everyone’s clarity:

* According to [Decree Law 84-C/2022|https://diariodarepublica.pt/dr/legislacao-consolidada/decreto-lei/2022-204709708] (article 27), *rent-a-car vehicle hire companies* must 
** +equip+ each of the vehicles in their fleet with on-board equipment;
** +adhere to a payment system+ though a +contract with Via Verde+ (ie the contract attached with Via Verde);
** include in the +vehicle rental contract+ with customers language regarding the sign up by the client to the service of automatic payment of tolls;
** +charge customers+ only the amount of tolls corresponding to their actual, *plus any administrative costs* (provided customers have used tolls and the amount of the administrative cost/fee is in accordance with regulation 343/2012, where it is defined the admin fee - [https://diariodarepublica.pt/dr/detalhe/portaria/343-2012-192439|https://diariodarepublica.pt/dr/detalhe/portaria/343-2012-192439]);
** +pay toll charges+ (ie be responsible for payment of toll charges and not a customer) for a given vehicle when:
*** A r+ental contract is not in force+ and there is use by that vehicle of road infrastructures which have an electronic toll system;
*** A +rental contract is in force+, but it has not been possible to obtain payment through this contract and subsequently the driver has not been identified by Via Verde. In this point b), rent-a-car companies shall send proof of the impossibility of obtaining payment to Via Verde, without which the identification of the driver cannot be accepted.
* Currently, Bolt has equipped the vehicles with the on-board equipment (let’s call it the “Via Verde IOT” to simplify) in the name of car-rental companies and therefore is processing payments to Via Verde on behalf of the partners.
* Consequently, Bolt is *currently* invoicing the “Via Verde IOT” costs to our customers on the behalf of Bolt or Via verde but not on the behalf of the car rental parnter. 
* *In the future* we would also like to be able to charge an admin fee for handling the via verde devices (just like most rental companies do).

I suggest that as next step [~accountid:625fb4921046bb0071ddf448] you share an example of invoice. This is importance since it is not clear who in named in the invoice, which is not necessary Bolt. Can you please provide an example?

With this information we can then clarify if the current step up in compliance with the t&c in place and fin reg, mainly that Bolt is not issuing a new fee but continues to act as a commercial agent of the partners. From local legal point of view this would appear fine and we would need to ensure contracts and t&c in place foresee this situation, provided it is also approved by the fin reg team. Therefore I am including in this review [~accountid:712020:822a759a-daf0-4161-afbf-8b79a2985fba] to have his view once we get the example of invoice.

Thank you.

